            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-MTSGdEFGaoK5gkxP9cOlbVIEgQe\">Looking at the electrical appliances, in 1920, washing machines were the most common, being present in about 40% of households, while refrigerators and vacuum cleaners were less prevalent, at approximately 3% and 30% respectively. Refrigerator ownership then rose dramatically to nearly 100% by 1980, maintaining this level until 2019. Similarly, vacuum cleaner usage showed a steady increase, reaching around 70% by 1960 and eventually matching refrigerator ownership by the end of the period. The proportion of homes with washing machines grew more modestly, rising to about 70% by 1960 and remaining relatively stable thereafter.</div>\n</div>",
