            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-WPzOdSnjkotAFvx6lmMlUwIZgBg\">Regarding housework hours, households in 1920 spent approximately 50 hours per week on tasks such as washing clothes, preparing meals, and cleaning. This figure decreased steadily over the following decades, falling to about 35 hours in 1940 and 20 hours by 1960. The downward trend continued, albeit more gradually, with weekly housework hours dropping to roughly 15 hours in 1980 and finally reaching about 10 hours in 2019.</div>\n</div>",
